[size=4][b]ARPG Movement 2.0.0 — Click, Hold, and Swap Tools Automatically[/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#ff5555]⚠ Requires MOMI 0.14.0 beta 3 or newer[/color][/b][/size]
[b]The MOMI version currently available on Nexus (0.13.x) cannot install this mod.[/b]
[b]Download the latest 0.14.0 beta from [url=https://github.com/Garethp/Mods-of-Mistria-Installer/releases]the MOMI GitHub releases page[/url][/b], then install the mod normally.

Move through Mistria with the mouse like an action RPG, click characters and objects to approach them, and let the game choose the right tool when you click a resource. WASD still works exactly as before and always takes control the moment you use it.

[size=3][b]What's new in 2.0.0[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Auto Tool Swapping[/b] — click a nearby rock, tree, stump, or dig spot and the correct tool is equipped automatically before your character acts.
[*][b]Smart interactions[/b] — click a distant NPC, chest, door, or other usable object and your character walks over and interacts with it.
[*][b]Mounted and swimming controls[/b] — hold right mouse to steer while riding or swimming too.
[*][b]Clear click feedback[/b] — a normal poof marks a valid destination; a red poof tells you when a click cannot be reached.
[*][b]Safer room movement[/b] — clicks outside a room no longer let the player walk past door transitions or leave the playable area.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Mouse controls[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Hold right mouse[/b] — steer toward the cursor. Your character walks when the cursor is close and runs when it is farther away. Hold your normal Walk control when you always want to walk.
[*][b]Tap right mouse on the ground[/b] — walk to that spot automatically, going around obstacles along the way.
[*][b]Tap right mouse on a character or object[/b] — walk into range and interact automatically. Nearby taps still work like the normal Interact button.
[*][b]WASD / jump / tool / E / Esc[/b] — immediately cancels a mouse-driven walk, so keyboard controls always win.
[/list]

While right mouse is held, Interact is temporarily suppressed. You can steer past people, chests, and doors without accidentally activating them.

[size=3][b]Auto Tool Swapping[/b][/size]
Auto Tool Swapping is enabled by default and uses the same left-click you already use for tools:
[list]
[*]Click a [b]rock[/b] to equip a pickaxe.
[*]Click a [b]tree or stump[/b] to equip an axe.
[*]Click a [b]dig spot[/b] to equip a shovel.
[*]In the [b]mines[/b], other action clicks equip a weapon when one is available.
[*]The mod searches your whole inventory and changes toolbar pages when necessary.
[*]It will not equip a tool that is too weak for the resource, and recognized resource clicks are left alone when the required tool is missing or out of reach.
[/list]

Press [b]F6[/b] to turn Auto Tool Swapping on or off. A notification confirms the change, and your choice is remembered. This feature only acts when left mouse is assigned to a normal tool-use control.

[size=3][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://github.com/Garethp/Mods-of-Mistria-Installer/releases]MOMI 0.14.0 beta 3 or newer[/url]. Until 0.14.0 reaches [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/fieldsofmistria/mods/78]the MOMI Nexus page[/url], the 0.13.x Nexus download cannot install this mod.
[*]Extract this mod into your [b]mods[/b] folder so the file is at [font=Courier New]mods/arpg_movement/manifest.json[/font].
[*]Run MOMI and install your mods.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
After the first launch, settings appear at [font=Courier New]%LOCALAPPDATA%\FieldsOfMistria\mod_data\arpg_movement\arpg_movement.json[/font]:
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]enabled[/font] — enable or disable the mod without uninstalling it
[*][font=Courier New]tap_seconds[/font] — maximum time for a press to count as a tap (default 0.6)
[*][font=Courier New]steer_start_seconds[/font] — delay before a hold begins steering (default 0.1)
[*][font=Courier New]walk_within_px[/font] / [font=Courier New]run_beyond_px[/font] — distances used to switch between walking and running (defaults 16 / 32)
[*][font=Courier New]interact_radius_px[/font] — distance where a ground tap stays a normal nearby interaction (default 24)
[*][font=Courier New]stop_within_px[/font] — standstill area around the player (default 8)
[*][font=Courier New]click_to_interact[/font] — walk to and use clicked characters and objects (default true)
[*][font=Courier New]click_marker[/font] — show the normal destination poof (default true)
[*][font=Courier New]invalid_click_marker[/font] — show a red poof for invalid destinations (default true)
[*][font=Courier New]auto_select_action_item[/font] — enable Auto Tool Swapping (default true; also toggled with F6)
[/list]

[size=3][b]Compatibility & notes[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Gamepad play is untouched.
[*]Cutscenes and scripted movement are untouched.
[*]Mounted taps keep their normal interaction behavior.
[*]Rebound movement, Walk, and cancellation controls are respected.
[*]If Interact is moved away from right mouse, right mouse simply becomes a dedicated movement button.
[*]Timing remains consistent at non-default frame-rate settings.
[/list]
